# Gokart — Hyperlocal Commerce Platform
# Environment setup guide
#
# Each microservice has its own .env file. Copy the matching .env.example
# in each folder to .env and configure values before starting services.
#
# Quick start (from repo root):
#   cp services/auth/.env.example      services/auth/.env
#   cp services/store/.env.example     services/store/.env
#   cp services/utils/.env.example     services/utils/.env
#   cp services/realtime/.env.example  services/realtime/.env
#   cp services/rider/.env.example     services/rider/.env
#   cp services/admin/.env.example     services/admin/.env
#   cp frontend/.env.example           frontend/.env
#
# ─── Shared values (must be identical across services) ───
#
# JWT_SEC
#   services/auth, store, rider, admin, realtime
#
# INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY
#   services/store, rider, utils, realtime, admin
#   frontend/.env → VITE_INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY
#
# RabbitMQ queue names (must match between producer and consumer)
#   PAYMENT_QUEUE        → utils (publish) + store (consume)
#   ORDER_READY_QUEUE    → store (publish) + rider (consume)
#
# ─── Service ports (default local) ───
#
#   Auth      5000   services/auth/.env.example
#   Store     5001   services/store/.env.example
#   Utils     5002   services/utils/.env.example
#   Realtime  5004   services/realtime/.env.example
#   Rider     5005   services/rider/.env.example
#   Admin     5006   services/admin/.env.example
#   Frontend  5173   frontend/.env.example
#
# ─── Infrastructure ───
#
#   MongoDB   mongodb://localhost:27017
#   RabbitMQ  amqp://localhost:5672  (management UI: http://localhost:15672)
#
# Start infrastructure with Docker:
#   docker compose up rabbitmq -d
